meta {
  name: Mark a tasting
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/produce/tastings/{{year}}/{{produceSlug}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "eatenOn": "{{year}}-06-14"
  }
}

docs {
  Record that the caller ate one produce item in one calendar year. One row per
  (user, slug, year), so this is an idempotent upsert: a repeat moves the date.

  eatenOn is required and comes from the client, in the caller's region's time
  zone. The server cannot default it, because its own "today" is UTC: at 8pm on
  December 31 in New York that is already January 1, the wrong year. The server
  checks it instead: it must fall in the path's year, be 2020-01-01 or later, and
  be no later than tomorrow in UTC (which admits every time zone).

  The slug must be kebab-case and at most 64 characters, and is not checked against
  the catalog. Because it is free text, each user is capped at 1,000 tastings in
  total; only a new row counts against the cap, so a date can still be corrected at
  the limit.

  - 200 the row `{ slug, year, eatenOn }`
  - 401 no or invalid token, or a valid token whose account has since been deleted
  - 409 at the 1,000 tasting limit
  - 422 malformed slug, a date outside the path's year, before 2020, or in the future
  - 429 over the write budget
}
